{
  "area": "mechanic-gameplay-state",
  "description": "The nine runtime gameplay-state predicates (packages/core/docs/mechanic-predicates.md §10.1) the mechanic rules read: health/3, energy/3, has_equipped/3, has_status/3, has_ability/2, near/3, at_location_type/2, level/2 and xp/3. The pack mirrored in each kb (packages/core/src/prolog/mechanics/gameplay-state-predicates.ts) declares them and defines nothing — so the contract these cases pin is that a world carrying none of them makes a query FAIL rather than raise existence_error, which is what lets an authored rule ask about state a save has not written yet. All nine are per-playthrough: they belong in save.currentState.prologFacts and never on a world template (§3).",
  "cases": [
    {
      "name": "reads-current-and-maximum-health",
      "kb": [
        ":- dynamic(health/3).",
        ":- dynamic(energy/3).",
        ":- dynamic(has_equipped/3).",
        ":- dynamic(has_status/3).",
        ":- dynamic(has_ability/2).",
        ":- dynamic(near/3).",
        ":- dynamic(at_location_type/2).",
        ":- dynamic(level/2).",
        ":- dynamic(xp/3).",
        ":- dynamic(gold/2).",
        "health(hero, 12, 30).",
        "energy(hero, 40, 100).",
        "has_equipped(hero, weapon, iron_sword).",
        "has_status(hero, poisoned, 30).",
        "has_ability(hero, second_wind).",
        "near(hero, wolf, 4).",
        "at_location_type(hero, cave).",
        "level(hero, 3).",
        "xp(hero, 250, 1000)."
      ],
      "query": "health(hero, C, M)",
      "expected": [
